<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario: the DataType-axis counterpart to
     test_vt_contradiction.NodeSet2 (which exercises the ValueRank axis).

     Declares two new custom DataTypes, CodeAType and CodeBType, as direct
     siblings under the real opcua:Enumeration (both rdfs:subClassOf
     Enumeration, neither a subtype of the other), so
     _add_datatype_disjointness asserts them pairwise disjoint. BaseType
     declares Mandatory "Code" : PropertyType/CodeAType. SubType overrides
     "Code" to PropertyType/CodeBType, a sibling, not a subtype, exactly
     the illegal move OPC UA's own DataType-override rule forbids (may only
     narrow to the same type or a subtype).

     VT(SubType, "Code") ends up subClassOf both:
       - [ onProperty sb:hasDataType; allValuesFrom CodeBType ] and
         [ onProperty sb:hasDataType; someValuesFrom CodeBType ]
       - VT(BaseType, "Code"), itself subClassOf the allValuesFrom/
         someValuesFrom pair for CodeAType

     sb:hasDataType is declared owl:FunctionalProperty (DataType is a
     Mandatory, single-valued Attribute of every real OPC UA Variable,
     per Part 3's Attributes table: not optional and not per-declaration
     like a ModellingRule), so someValuesFrom is correct here even though
     it would be wrong on the containment property (see
     _add_all_values_from's own comment). Functional + someValuesFrom(A)
     + someValuesFrom(B) with A/B disjoint forces a genuine contradiction:
     the (at most one) hasDataType value would have to be simultaneously
     in CodeAType and CodeBType. Before this fix, only allValuesFrom was
     asserted, which is vacuously satisfiable by zero hasDataType edges,
     confirmed consistent by real HermiT: a genuine detection gap relative
     to the ValueRank axis (whose symbolic classes are asserted via a
     direct, unconditional rdfs:subClassOf edge, not a property
     restriction). Now confirmed UNSATISFIABLE by real HermiT
     (check_consistency.py), matching the ValueRank case. -->
